{"id": "packet.json", "pointer": "", "view": "value", "value": {"contract_version": 2, "case_id": "geometry-product-dimension", "graph_sha256": "721031e69a0b2ed2da4b4441595cfbeba55696f852b815dc278f3fcb12e98c2e", "spec_sha256": "8a9a7e15cc0bf2be2dcd525bc78f1e24947ca2830bcbe3c25525e9aef284accc", "parameters": [{"symbol": "n", "type": "natural number"}, {"symbol": "E", "type": "subset of Euclidean ℝ^n"}], "logic": {"classical": true, "rules": ["direct", "case_elimination", "forall_introduction", "implication_introduction", "exists_elimination"], "calculations": ["equality: Equality reflexivity, symmetry, transitivity and substitution.", "definitions: Unfold an explicitly supplied definition; this proves no extra property.", "finite_algebra: Routine finite semiring/ring/field arithmetic, including zero/one laws, distributivity, associativity and finite polynomial identities. Correct elementary compression is permitted; a substantive missing argument is not.", "finite_order: Routine ordered-field reasoning with actual signs/domains: order laws, adding inequalities, multiplication/division with sign conditions, and real square nonnegativity. Ordinary valid elementary inferences need no exhaustive displayed chain. Check that the conclusion follows; substantial named theorems still require inputs or verified-background admission.", "finite_sums: Unfold and rearrange finite sums/products with explicitly given finite indices."], "primitives": [{"symbol": "0", "type": "typed numeral", "meaning": "Zero of the explicitly specified mathematical type."}, {"symbol": "1", "type": "typed numeral", "meaning": "One of the explicitly specified mathematical type."}, {"symbol": "2", "type": "typed numeral", "meaning": "Two of the explicitly specified mathematical type, including an exponent two."}, {"symbol": "ℕ", "type": "number system", "meaning": "The natural numbers with their usual arithmetic."}, {"symbol": "ℤ", "type": "number system", "meaning": "The integers with their usual arithmetic."}, {"symbol": "ℚ", "type": "number system", "meaning": "The rational numbers with their usual ordered-field operations."}, {"symbol": "ℝ", "type": "number system", "meaning": "The real numbers with their usual ordered-field structure."}, {"symbol": "ℂ", "type": "number system", "meaning": "The complex numbers with their usual field structure."}, {"symbol": "∅", "type": "typed set notation", "meaning": "The empty set in the explicitly specified ambient type."}, {"symbol": "∞", "type": "typed order notation", "meaning": "The top element in an explicitly specified extended ordered codomain."}, {"symbol": "norm", "type": "norm notation", "meaning": "The norm supplied by the explicitly specified normed-space structure; no estimate is granted."}, {"symbol": "∂", "type": "derivative notation", "meaning": "Classical differentiation where the stated derivative exists; no calculus rule is granted."}, {"symbol": "∫", "type": "integral notation", "meaning": "The integral for the explicitly specified function, measure and codomain; no integral identity is granted."}, {"symbol": "Integrable", "type": "predicate notation", "meaning": "Bochner integrability for the specified function and measure; no integrability is asserted."}, {"symbol": "AEStronglyMeasurable", "type": "predicate notation", "meaning": "Almost-everywhere strong measurability for the specified function and measure; no measurability is asserted."}]}, "pins": {"lean_version": "4.32.2", "mathlib_commit": "905b95818eb32af7874a58b427f50c1711a5e96c", "mathlib_root": "/Users/syyui/formalization-tools/lean-mathlib-v4.32.2/mathlib"}, "foundation_profile": "finite-language-3", "standard_language": "Ordinary typed mathematical language: logical connectives, quantifiers, equality, sets, functions, tuples, finite indices and their usual notation. A type explicitly named natural numbers, integers, rationals, reals or complex numbers means that standard structure, with its usual numerals and arithmetic operations; these operation tokens need not be redeclared as project objects. The fixed finite calculation rules below, including a+0=a, are controller permissions, not an author claim. Project functions/sets and substantive analytic properties still need their explicit declarations and direct inputs or displayed local proofs.", "background_policy": "verified-background-1", "definitions": [{"id": "D001", "symbol": "I", "type": "subset of ℝ", "definition": "I=[0,1]={t∈ℝ:0≤t≤1}.", "depends_on": [], "requires": [], "binders": [], "objects": []}, {"id": "D002", "symbol": "F", "type": "subset of Euclidean ℝ^{n+1}, identified with ℝ^n×ℝ", "definition": "F=E×I. Under the coordinate identification (x,t)↔(x_1,…,x_n,t), the distance between (x,t) and (y,u) is sqrt(‖x-y‖₂²+|t-u|²). For n=0, ℝ^0 consists of its unique empty coordinate vector.", "depends_on": ["D001"], "requires": [], "binders": [{"symbol": "x", "type": "point of ℝ^n"}, {"symbol": "y", "type": "point of ℝ^n"}, {"symbol": "t", "type": "real number"}, {"symbol": "u", "type": "real number"}], "objects": ["n", "E", "I", "x", "y", "t", "u"]}, {"id": "D003", "symbol": "Hscale", "type": "operator on a metric space X, a positive real s, a positive real δ and a subset A⊆X, valued in [0,∞]", "definition": "For a metric space X, s>0, δ>0 and A⊆X, Hscale(s,δ,A)=inf{Σ_{i≥0}(diam U_i)^s : A⊆⋃_{i≥0}U_i and diam U_i≤δ for every i}. Covers are countable (finite covers are padded by empty sets). The diameter is the supremum of pairwise distances, with diameter of the empty set zero and unbounded diameter +∞; an empty member contributes zero. Sums, infima and suprema are in [0,∞], with inf ∅=∞. Covers are not required to be measurable.", "depends_on": [], "requires": [], "binders": [{"symbol": "X", "type": "metric space"}, {"symbol": "s", "type": "positive real"}, {"symbol": "δ", "type": "positive real"}, {"symbol": "A", "type": "subset of X"}, {"symbol": "U", "type": "sequence of subsets of X"}], "objects": ["X", "s", "δ", "A", "U"]}, {"id": "D005", "symbol": "hdim", "type": "operator on subsets of extended metric spaces, valued in [0,∞]", "definition": "For A⊆X, hdim(A)=sup{a∈[0,∞):Hnative(a,A)=∞}, with the empty supremum equal to zero and real exponents embedded into [0,∞]. This is the native dimH definition (the exponent is represented by a nonnegative real). It is the usual Hausdorff dimension; in particular the definition assigns zero to the empty set.", "depends_on": ["D008"], "requires": [], "binders": [{"symbol": "X", "type": "extended metric space"}, {"symbol": "A", "type": "subset of X"}], "objects": ["X", "A", "Hnative"]}, {"id": "D006", "symbol": "D", "type": "extended nonnegative real number", "definition": "D=hdim(E). Once finiteness is proved, real arithmetic with D means its unique finite real representative; no finiteness is assumed by this definition.", "depends_on": ["D005"], "requires": [], "binders": [], "objects": ["E", "hdim"]}, {"id": "D008", "symbol": "Hnative", "type": "operator on a real exponent a and a subset A of an extended metric space X with its Borel measurable structure, valued in [0,∞]", "definition": "Hnative(a,A) denotes the native value (MeasureTheory.Measure.hausdorffMeasure a)(A) on X. Its full covering formula is sup_{r∈(0,∞]} inf_{T:ℕ→Set X, A⊆⋃_i T_i, ∀i ediam(T_i)≤r} Σ_i w_a(T_i), where w_a(T)=0 for T empty and w_a(T)=(ediam T)^a otherwise; all diameters and operations here are extended nonnegative real operations, including extended real powers. Thus empty sets are zero even at exponent zero. The native definition is the Borel measure Measure.mkMetric(r↦r^a). For ordinary metric spaces ediam is the extended-valued supremum of ordinary distances.", "depends_on": [], "requires": [], "binders": [{"symbol": "X", "type": "extended metric space"}, {"symbol": "a", "type": "real number"}, {"symbol": "A", "type": "subset of X"}], "objects": ["X", "a", "A"]}], "inputs": [{"id": "N002", "kind": "internal", "statement": "E is bounded. For every δ>0 and every s>0, E has a finite cover by sets of diameter at most δ and finite s-cost, so Hscale(s,δ,E)<∞. Also 0≤D≤n, in particular hdim(E)=D is finite and can be identified with a real number. If n=0, then E=ℝ^0 is the singleton and D=0.", "definitions": ["D003", "D005", "D006"], "binders": [{"symbol": "δ", "type": "positive real"}, {"symbol": "s", "type": "positive real"}], "objects": ["E", "n", "δ", "s", "D", "Hscale", "hdim"]}, {"id": "M005", "kind": "mathlib", "statement": "Let α be a measurable space, μ a measure on α, β a countable type and f:β→α→[0,∞]. If every f_i is μ-almost-everywhere measurable, then ∫⁻_α Σ_{i:β} f_i(a) dμ(a)=Σ_{i:β} ∫⁻_α f_i(a) dμ(a).", "definitions": [], "binders": [{"symbol": "α", "type": "measurable space"}, {"symbol": "μ", "type": "measure on α"}, {"symbol": "β", "type": "countable type"}, {"symbol": "f", "type": "β→α→[0,∞]"}], "objects": ["α", "μ", "β", "f"], "source_contract": {"hypotheses": ["α has a measurable space structure and μ is a measure on it.", "β is countable.", "For every i∈β, f_i is μ-almost-everywhere measurable."], "declaration": "MeasureTheory.lintegral_tsum", "signature": "@MeasureTheory.lintegral_tsum : ∀ {α : Type u_1} {β : Type u_2} {m : MeasurableSpace.{u_1} α} {μ : MeasureTheory.Measure.{u_1} α}
  [Countable.{u_2 + 1} β] {f : β → α → ENNReal},
  (∀ (i : β), AEMeasurable.{u_1, 0} (f i) μ) →
    Eq.{1} (∫⁻ (a : α), ∑' (i : β), f i a ∂μ) (∑' (i : β), ∫⁻ (a : α), f i a ∂μ)"}}, {"id": "M007", "kind": "mathlib", "statement": "For any real endpoints a,b, Lebesgue measure of the closed interval [a,b] is ENNReal.ofReal(b-a), namely max(b-a,0) embedded in [0,∞].", "definitions": [], "binders": [{"symbol": "a", "type": "real number"}, {"symbol": "b", "type": "real number"}], "objects": ["a", "b"], "source_contract": {"hypotheses": [], "declaration": "Real.volume_Icc", "signature": "@Real.volume_Icc : ∀ {a b : ℝ}, Eq.{1} (MeasureTheory.volume.{0} (Set.Icc.{0} a b)) (ENNReal.ofReal (HSub.hSub.{0, 0, 0} b a))"}}, {"id": "M008", "kind": "mathlib", "statement": "For any real endpoints a,b, Lebesgue measure of the open interval (a,b) is ENNReal.ofReal(b-a), namely max(b-a,0) embedded in [0,∞].", "definitions": [], "binders": [{"symbol": "a", "type": "real number"}, {"symbol": "b", "type": "real number"}], "objects": ["a", "b"], "source_contract": {"hypotheses": [], "declaration": "Real.volume_Ioo", "signature": "@Real.volume_Ioo : ∀ {a b : ℝ}, Eq.{1} (MeasureTheory.volume.{0} (Set.Ioo.{0} a b)) (ENNReal.ofReal (HSub.hSub.{0, 0, 0} b a))"}}], "output": {"id": "N004", "kind": "internal", "statement": "For every real s>0 and every real δ>0, Hscale(s,δ,E)≤Hscale(s+1,δ,F).", "definitions": ["D002", "D003"], "binders": [{"symbol": "s", "type": "positive real"}, {"symbol": "δ", "type": "positive real"}], "objects": ["s", "δ", "E", "F", "Hscale"]}, "inference": {"id": "R004", "inputs": ["N002", "M005", "M007", "M008"], "output": "N004", "definitions": ["D001", "D002", "D003"], "rules": ["direct", "forall_introduction", "implication_introduction"], "locals": [{"symbol": "s", "type": "real number", "scope": "R004/argument", "start": "S001", "end": "S005", "kind": "arbitrary", "declaration": "Fix s>0.", "from_inputs": [], "from_local": [], "objects": []}, {"symbol": "δ", "type": "real number", "scope": "R004/argument", "start": "S001", "end": "S005", "kind": "arbitrary", "declaration": "Fix δ>0.", "from_inputs": [], "from_local": [], "objects": []}, {"symbol": "ε", "type": "real number", "scope": "R004/argument", "start": "S001", "end": "S005", "kind": "arbitrary", "declaration": "Fix ε>0, to be sent to zero.", "from_inputs": [], "from_local": [], "objects": []}, {"symbol": "c", "type": "extended nonnegative real number", "scope": "R004/argument", "start": "S001", "end": "S005", "kind": "definition", "declaration": "Define c=Hscale(s,δ,E).", "from_inputs": [], "from_local": [], "objects": ["Hscale", "s", "δ", "E"]}, {"symbol": "V", "type": "sequence of subsets of ℝ^{n+1}", "scope": "R004/arbitrary-cover", "start": "S002", "end": "S005", "kind": "arbitrary", "declaration": "Take any countable δ-cover V of F, allowing empty padding members.", "from_inputs": [], "from_local": [], "objects": ["n", "δ", "F"]}, {"symbol": "ρ", "type": "sequence of finite nonnegative real numbers", "scope": "R004/arbitrary-cover", "start": "S002", "end": "S005", "kind": "definition", "declaration": "Define ρ_i=diam V_i; since V is a δ-cover, 0≤ρ_i≤δ.", "from_inputs": [], "from_local": [], "objects": ["V", "δ"]}, {"symbol": "A_i", "type": "sequence of subsets of ℝ^n", "scope": "R004/arbitrary-cover", "start": "S002", "end": "S005", "kind": "definition", "declaration": "Define A_i as the projection of V_i onto ℝ^n.", "from_inputs": [], "from_local": [], "objects": ["V", "n"]}, {"symbol": "B_i", "type": "sequence of subsets of ℝ", "scope": "R004/arbitrary-cover", "start": "S002", "end": "S005", "kind": "definition", "declaration": "Define B_i as the last-coordinate projection of V_i.", "from_inputs": [], "from_local": [], "objects": ["V"]}, {"symbol": "η", "type": "sequence of positive real numbers", "scope": "R004/arbitrary-cover", "start": "S002", "end": "S005", "kind": "definition", "declaration": "Define η_i=ε2^{-i-1}/(1+ρ_i^s).", "from_inputs": [], "from_local": [], "objects": ["ε", "ρ", "s"]}, {"symbol": "J", "type": "sequence of open subsets of ℝ, each empty or a bounded open interval", "scope": "R004/arbitrary-cover", "start": "S002", "end": "S005", "kind": "definition", "declaration": "If V_i is nonempty, set J_i=(inf B_i-η_i/2,sup B_i+η_i/2); otherwise set J_i=∅.", "from_inputs": [], "from_local": [], "objects": ["V", "B_i", "η"]}, {"symbol": "f", "type": "ℕ→ℝ→[0,∞]", "scope": "R004/arbitrary-cover", "start": "S003", "end": "S005", "kind": "definition", "declaration": "Define f_i(t)=ρ_i^s 1_{J_i}(t), with the nonnegative real coefficient embedded in [0,∞].", "from_inputs": [], "from_local": [], "objects": ["ρ", "s", "J"]}], "argument": [{"id": "S001", "text": "Fix s>0, δ>0 and ε>0. Define c=Hscale(s,δ,E). N002 gives a finite δ-cover of E with finite s-cost, so c<∞. Thus c can be integrated as a finite nonnegative constant.", "uses": ["N002"], "uses_local": [], "objects": ["s", "δ", "ε", "c", "E", "Hscale"], "produces": [{"id": "F001", "statement": "c=Hscale(s,δ,E)<∞.", "binders": [], "objects": ["c", "Hscale", "s", "δ", "E"], "assumptions": ["L1"]}], "introduces": ["L1"], "discharges": []}, {"id": "S002", "text": "Take any countable δ-cover V of F and write ρ_i=diam V_i, A_i=π_{ℝ^n}(V_i), B_i=π_ℝ(V_i). Coordinate projections decrease distances by the Euclidean distance formula; therefore diam A_i≤ρ_i and diam B_i≤ρ_i≤δ. Set η_i=ε2^{-i-1}/(1+ρ_i^s)>0. For every nonempty V_i its projection B_i is nonempty and bounded: distances between all its points are at most δ, so its infimum and supremum are finite. Their difference is at most ρ_i. Define J_i=(inf B_i-η_i/2,sup B_i+η_i/2), which contains B_i and has length at most ρ_i+η_i. For empty V_i set J_i=∅; such members have ρ_i^s=0 and are harmless. This is the same as discarding empty members while retaining the original indices. Thus every J_i is open and B_i⊆J_i. Neither V_i nor its projections need be measurable.", "uses": [], "uses_local": [], "objects": ["V", "F", "δ", "ρ", "A_i", "B_i", "η", "ε", "s", "J", "n", "c"], "produces": [{"id": "F002", "statement": "For every i, diam A_i≤ρ_i≤δ, B_i⊆J_i, and J_i is either empty or an open interval of length at most ρ_i+η_i; η_i=ε2^{-i-1}/(1+ρ_i^s)>0.", "binders": [], "objects": ["A_i", "B_i", "J", "ρ", "δ", "η", "ε", "s"], "assumptions": ["L1", "L2"]}], "introduces": ["L2"], "discharges": []}, {"id": "S003", "text": "For any t∈I, the A_i with t∈J_i cover E: for any x∈E some V_i contains (x,t), and then x∈A_i and t∈B_i⊆J_i. By F002 this is a δ-cover, whose s-cost is at most Σ_iρ_i^s 1_{J_i}(t). Hence c≤Σ_iρ_i^s 1_{J_i}(t) for every t∈I. Define f_i(t)=ρ_i^s 1_{J_i}(t). Every f_i is nonnegative and Borel measurable because J_i is open and its coefficient is a fixed finite nonnegative real. In particular it is almost-everywhere measurable for Lebesgue measure restricted to I.", "uses": [], "uses_local": ["F001", "F002"], "objects": ["c", "E", "I", "F", "V", "A_i", "B_i", "J", "ρ", "s", "δ", "f"], "produces": [{"id": "F003", "statement": "For every t∈I, c≤Σ_i f_i(t), where f_i(t)=ρ_i^s1_{J_i}(t); each f_i is Borel measurable and hence Lebesgue-almost-everywhere measurable for the restricted measure on I.", "binders": [{"symbol": "t", "type": "real number in I"}], "objects": ["t", "I", "c", "f", "ρ", "s", "J"], "assumptions": ["L1", "L2"]}], "introduces": [], "discharges": []}, {"id": "S004", "text": "Integrate F003 against Lebesgue measure restricted to I. Its total mass is one by M007 with endpoints 0,1. Monotonicity of the nonnegative integral, the integral of a constant, and M005 applied to the nonnegative measurable series yield c≤Σ_i∫_I f_i(t)dt=Σ_iρ_i^s|J_i∩I|. Here the integral of a constant times a measurable indicator is that constant times its set's measure, directly the simple-function integral formula. By M008 and monotonicity of measure, |J_i∩I|≤|J_i|≤ρ_i+η_i (the empty case is zero). Consequently c≤Σ_iρ_i^s|J_i∩I|≤Σ_iρ_i^{s+1}+Σ_iη_iρ_i^s≤Σ_iρ_i^{s+1}+ε, because η_iρ_i^s=ε2^{-i-1}ρ_i^s/(1+ρ_i^s)≤ε2^{-i-1} and Σ_{i≥0}2^{-i-1}=1. All series are nonnegative; their order comparisons and splitting are valid also when a sum is infinite.", "uses": ["M005", "M007", "M008"], "uses_local": ["F001", "F002", "F003"], "objects": ["c", "I", "f", "J", "ρ", "η", "s", "ε"], "produces": [{"id": "F004", "statement": "c≤Σ_iρ_i^{s+1}+ε for the arbitrary δ-cover V and arbitrary ε>0.", "binders": [], "objects": ["c", "ρ", "s", "ε", "V", "δ"], "assumptions": ["L1", "L2"]}], "introduces": [], "discharges": []}, {"id": "S005", "text": "If Σ_iρ_i^{s+1}=∞, the desired bound c≤Σ_iρ_i^{s+1} is immediate. If the sum is finite, F004 for all ε>0 gives that bound by letting ε↓0. Since V was any δ-cover of F, taking the infimum of its (s+1)-costs gives Hscale(s,δ,E)=c≤Hscale(s+1,δ,F). The construction of J depended on ε, but c and this cover's cost did not, so the limit is legitimate. Discharge the arbitrary-cover restrictions and s>0,δ>0,ε>0 restrictions and universally quantify s,δ. This proves the slicing inequality.", "uses": [], "uses_local": ["F001", "F004"], "objects": ["V", "ρ", "s", "δ", "ε", "c", "E", "F", "J", "Hscale"], "produces": [], "introduces": [], "discharges": ["L2", "L1"]}], "applications": [{"input": "M005", "at": "S004", "bindings": "Set α=ℝ with its Borel measurable structure, μ=Lebesgue measure restricted to I, β=ℕ and use f_i from S003.", "hypothesis_checks": ["Lebesgue measure restricted to the Borel set I is a measure on this measurable space.", "The series index is ℕ, a countable type.", "F003 proves Borel measurability of every f_i, hence almost-everywhere measurability for μ."]}, {"input": "M007", "at": "S004", "bindings": "Set a=0 and b=1; the interval [a,b] is I.", "hypothesis_checks": []}, {"input": "M008", "at": "S004", "bindings": "For each nonempty V_i set a=inf B_i-η_i/2 and b=sup B_i+η_i/2, so (a,b)=J_i; empty members contribute zero separately.", "hypothesis_checks": []}]}, "warning": "Direct inputs and fixed logic are supplied. Audit A may record positively checked routine background under the declared policy, with logged pinned-library evidence. No ancestor proof or extra H is available. A packet is not an audit certificate.", "packet_sha256": "132081655929420e9f2ffcff69ab708726f56a708857d2abdeb102867cfbfbf0"}, "has_more": false, "next_offset": null}

