eration tokens need not be redeclared as project objects. The fixed finite calculation rules below, including a+0=a, are controller permissions, not an author claim. Project functions/sets and substantive analytic properties still need their explicit declarations and direct inputs or displayed local proofs.", "background_policy": "verified-background-1", "definitions": [{"id": "D001", "symbol": "I", "type": "subset of ℝ", "definition": "I=[0,1]={t∈ℝ:0≤t≤1}.", "depends_on": [], "requires": [], "binders": [], "objects": []}, {"id": "D002", "symbol": "F", "type": "subset of Euclidean ℝ^{n+1}, identified with ℝ^n×ℝ", "definition": "F=E×I. Under the coordinate identification (x,t)↔(x_1,…,x_n,t), the distance between (x,t) and (y,u) is sqrt(‖x-y‖₂²+|t-u|²). For n=0, ℝ^0 consists of its unique empty coordinate vector.", "depends_on": ["D001"], "requires": [], "binders": [{"symbol": "x", "type": "point of ℝ^n"}, {"symbol": "y", "type": "point of ℝ^n"}, {"symbol": "t", "type": "real number"}, {"symbol": "u", "type": "real number"}], "objects": ["n", "E", "I", "x", "y", "t", "u"]}, {"id": "D003", "symbol": "Hscale", "type": "operator on a metric space X, a positive real s, a positive real δ and a subset A⊆X, valued in [0,∞]", "definition": "For a metric space X, s>0, δ>0 and A⊆X, Hscale(s,δ,A)=inf{Σ_{i≥0}(diam U_i)^s : A⊆⋃_{i≥0}U_i and diam U_i≤δ for every i}. Covers are countable (finite covers are padded by empty sets). The diameter is the supremum of pairwise distances, with diameter of the empty set zero and unbounded diameter +∞; an empty member contributes zero. Sums, infima and suprema are in [0,∞], with inf ∅=∞. Covers are not required to be measurable.", "depends_on": [], "requires": [], "binders": [{"symbol": "X", "type": "metric space"}, {"symbol": "s", "type": "positive real"}, {"symbol": "δ", "type": "positive real"}, {"symbol": "A", "type": "subset of X"}, {"symbol": "U", "type": "sequence of subsets of X"}], "objects": ["X", "s", "δ", "A", "U"]}, {"id": "D005", "symbol": "hdim", "type": "operator on subsets of extended metric spaces, valued in [0,∞]", "definition": "For A⊆X, hdim(A)=sup{a∈[0,∞):Hnative(a,A)=∞}, with the empty supremum equal to zero and real exponents embedded into [0,∞]. This is the native dimH definition (the exponent is represented by a nonnegative real). It is the usual Hausdorff dimension; in particular the definition assigns zero to the empty set.", "depends_on": ["D008"], "requires": [], "binders": [{"symbol": "X", "type": "extended metric space"}, {"symbol": "A", "type": "subset of X"}], "objects": ["X", "A", "Hnative"]}, {"id": "D006", "symbol": "D", "type": "extended nonnegative real number", "definition": "D=hdim(E). Once finiteness is proved, real arithmetic with D means its unique finite real representative; no finiteness is assumed by this definition.", "depends_on": ["D005"], "requires": [], "binders": [], "objects": ["E", "hdim"]}, {"id": "D008", "symbol": "Hnative", "type": "operator on a real exponent a and a subset A of an extended metric space X with its Borel measurable structure, valued in [0,∞]", "definition": "Hnative(a,A) denotes the native value (MeasureTheory.Measure.hausdorffMeasure a)(A) on X. Its full covering formula is sup_{r∈(0,∞]} inf_{T:ℕ→Set X, A⊆⋃_i T_i, ∀i ediam(T_i)≤r} Σ_i w_a(T_i), where w_a(T)=0 for T empty and w_a(T)=(ediam T)^a otherwise; all diameters and operations here are extended nonnegative real operations, including extended real powers. Thus empty sets are zero even at exponent zero. The native definition is the Borel measure Measure.mkMetric(r↦r^a). For ordinary metric spaces ediam is the extended-valued supremum of ordinary distances.", "depends_on": [], "requires": [], "binders": [{"symbol": "X", "type": "extended metric space"}, {"symbol": "a", "type": "real number"}, {"symbol": "A", "type": "subset of X"}], "objects": ["X", "a", "A"]}], "inputs": [{"id": "N002", "kind": "internal", "statement": "E is bounded. For every δ>0 and every s>0, E has a finite cover by sets of diameter at most δ and finite s-cost, so Hscale(s,δ,E)<∞. Also 0≤D≤n, in particular hdim(E)=D is finite and can be identified with a real number. If n=0, then E=ℝ^0 is the singleton and D=0.", "definitions": ["D003", "D005", "D006"], "binders": [{"symbol": "δ", "type": "positive real"}, {"symbol": "s", "type": "positive real"}], "objects": ["E", "n", "δ", "s", "D", "Hscale", "hdim"]}, {"id": "M005", "kind": "mathlib", "statement": "Let α be a measurable space, μ a measure on α, β a countable type and f:β→α→[0,∞]. If every f_i is μ-almost-everywhere measurable, then ∫⁻_α Σ_{i:β} f_i(a) dμ(a)=Σ_{i:β} ∫⁻_α f_i(a) dμ(a).", "definitions": [], "binders": [{"symbol": "α", "type": "measurable space"}, {"symbol": "μ", "type": "measure on α"}, {"symbol": "β", "type": "countable type"}, {"symbol": "f", "type": "β→α→[0,∞]"}], "objects": ["α", "μ", "β", "f"], "source_contract": {"hypotheses": ["α has a measurable space structure and μ is a measure on it.", "β is countable.", "For every i∈β, f_i is μ-almost-everywhere measurable."], "declaration": "MeasureTheory.lintegral_tsum", "signature": "@MeasureTheory.lintegral_tsum : ∀ {α : Type u_1} {β : Type u_2} {m : MeasurableSpace.{u_1} α} {μ : MeasureTheory.Measure.{u_1} α}
  [Countable.{u_2 + 1} β] {f : β → α → ENNReal},
